# Immutable factories & defensive copies

## The `of` factories (Java 9+)

```java
List<String> colors = List.of("red", "green", "blue");
Set<String>  tags   = Set.of("java", "jvm");
Map<String, Integer> m = Map.of("a", 1, "b", 2);
```

- **Truly immutable** — `add`/`put` throws
- **Null-hostile**; `Set.of`/`Map.of` reject duplicates
- Snapshot an existing one: `List.copyOf(other)`

## View vs copy — don't confuse them

```java
var view = Collections.unmodifiableList(live);  // window
live.add("c");   // ← shows through the view!
var snap = List.copyOf(live);                   // independent
live.add("d");   // ← snap unaffected
```

Want a real guarantee? **Copy**, not a view.

## Defensive copies

```java
public Team(List<String> members) {
    this.members = List.copyOf(members);   // copy IN
}
```

Copy **in** at the boundary; return immutable/view **out**. Prevents leaks of internal state.
